cygwin: don't add .exe to sys.executable if the path already works

"/usr/bin/python" resolves without the suffix on Cygwin, so a child started
with sys.executable reported a different name than its parent, which broke
the usage messages of argparse and tabnanny.

--- Python-3.14.10.orig/Modules/getpath.py
+++ Python-3.14.10/Modules/getpath.py
@@ -248,7 +248,8 @@
 if not program_name:
     program_name = DEFAULT_PROGRAM_NAME
 
-if EXE_SUFFIX and not hassuffix(program_name, EXE_SUFFIX) and isxfile(program_name + EXE_SUFFIX):
+if (EXE_SUFFIX and not hassuffix(program_name, EXE_SUFFIX) and not isxfile(program_name)
+    and isxfile(program_name + EXE_SUFFIX)):
     program_name = program_name + EXE_SUFFIX
 
 
